## How it was tested

- `HunterRumoursTest` (new, `content:skills:hunter` integration, 7 tests): turn-in XP matches the wiki ranges; assignments follow each hunter's list, level and other hunters; rumours need their quest and Herblore level; catches reach the rare part by the pity threshold and the whistle names it; a pity part is destroyed when the inventory is full and comes on the next catch; turn-in swaps the part for the loot sack once; with back-to-back off the rumour just handed in is not offered again.
- `HunterGuildScriptTest` (new, 5 tests): assignment and remember lines say "one of", "some of" or "its" as the transcripts do; Wolf's leave option is "Never mind." and the player says "See you later."; buying a stew swaps exactly 20 coins for one stew; too few coins moves nothing; a full inventory with coins left over moves nothing, exact coins free their slot.
- `ButterflyScriptTest` gains one test (7 in all): a magic net catch counts for the rumour.
- Fork CI (GitHub Actions: freshCache, buildCache, assemble test integration, boot) green at the commit.
- Not re-checked in game on this commit; the same dialogues were checked on the Android device with the Hunters' Rumours hub plugin on an earlier build of fin/hunter (assign, remind, hand-in), see server-handoff.md on the fork's docs branch.

